From 0a17c656ee27eaa0e82a1311c042db59f4712f5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 21:19:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Put the redesign into the renderers instead of beside them

Pip and the plates had been sitting in the package unused while every rendered
post still came out in the old design. This wires the design in.

Surface. The palette flips from near-black to paper. Every post used to sit on
#141210, which made the profile grid read as one dark smudge and put a warm
terracotta identity on a ground that fought it. Feed presence comes from
contrast at the edge of the post, and paper against Instagram's white chrome
separates cleanly. The three background builders - panel_gradient,
brand_fallback, cinematic_scrim - all assumed a dark ground and produced dark
plates under dark type once the tokens moved, so they now return paper and the
old bodies are kept as _legacy_ for the photo-backed paths.

Display face. title_font was Anton: free, ubiquitous, the default face of every
automated news account, and single-weight - so nothing could be emphasised
inside a headline. It is Manrope's weight axis now, which is also what makes
kinetic reel type possible. Verified live: 200/400/600/800 render at measurably
different widths.

Furniture. The category pill was the loudest object on the canvas carrying the
least useful information there; it is a coloured rule under the wordmark now.
The ghosted "01" is gone - it sat at an opacity that read as a compression
fault, numbering a sequence Instagram already numbers. The SWIPE hint is gone
for the same reason. Drop shadows default off: they existed to hold type over
photography on dark, and on paper they read as a blurred edge.

Pip appears on the story card, on story slides and on the CTA, placed from the
measured bottom of the header rather than a fixed y - the header grows with the
headline, so any guessed position eventually lands on the standfirst, which is
exactly what the first two attempts did. Sensitive stories get no mascot:
theme.pose_for returns None and the caller draws nothing.

Category accents darkened for the new ground. All four now clear 4.5:1 on paper;
the old values were tuned against near-black and failed.

219/219 tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
